✅ 3. K-Means Clustering
Concept

K-Means partitions the dataset into K clusters by minimizing the within-cluster sum of squares (WCSS).

Algorithm Steps

Select K (number of clusters).

Initialize K centroids randomly.

Assign each data point to the closest centroid (Euclidean distance).

Recalculate centroids based on assigned points.

Repeat steps 3–4 until convergence.

